title Two readings of what prose is -- the grading card was blind to the two forms this tree's own rules ask for
prompt The baton: open the round, honor the card, reds first, close on a check-in.
rota lap 4288, row 3 was water and my own last lap read it, so advanced by hand to row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in. Threshold read whole, then the fixed seat context/TWO_ROOMS.md. Earth's instruction is to take the concrete fact at the door before arguing with it, so the lap RAN two_rooms_doorway_scan.sh rather than reading about the census. It answered fails=3 against ceiling=3, all three dated testimony on active-designing/date/20260820/, and the scan's own head already reasons that 3 is a floor rather than a target. The write-time loom the baton's DOOR clause was seated for (two_rooms_doorway_touch_scan.sh) already stands and gates a newly added page at zero. The reading closed a concern rather than opening work, which is the honest outcome, so the lap went to the oldest open red in its own lane. It also confirmed by first-hand run that the Kin line my last lap gated reads correctly on the earth threshold page.
think Cold roster first, held still while it ran: 189 guards, 1455s, 186 green, 0 red, 3 gated at custody, tree_moved=no. Checked fleet_call for a foreign runner in this tree (none) and matched the runner's stashed_entries=6 and its six stash detail lines against git stash list here, per the baton's clause seated from %620.
think Reds first. Of the rows on the pin, %574 is squarely this lane: Reach in tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh spells an elder line pattern that prose_register_scan.sh replaced, so the two readings of one card disagree about which lines are prose.
think The card already reports the gap rather than scoring it, and its own comment refuses to widen the reading in one unmeasured step. So the lap's first job was to measure, not to edit: build the population the card's own scan grades (45 pages across the door, teaching and candidate rosters, read out of prose_register_scan.sh) and compare composite against composite_shadow, which the card already publishes.
think The shadow reading costs mean -1.42 across 45 pages, 19 down and 7 up, and crosses no page below the B door. That answers the standing question. Yet 7 pages RISING under a reading everyone calls stricter is a tell that the delta is a net rather than a direction.
think Diffing the two line filters on the worst faller (lotus/README.md) showed why. The register rule admits two different kinds: genuine bold-led prose paragraphs, and **Key:** header lines that carry no sentence. Counting both across the 45: 232 header lines against 155 bold-led prose lines, on 44 of 45 pages. Adopting the shadow wholesale would let in more noise than signal, by count.
think Diffing mandate/README.md, which has no bold-led prose yet still moved, found the second blindness nobody had named: the italic radiant wish that closes an earned page. The elder pattern skipped a marker ALONE, so one asterisk before a capital read as a bullet. That is 55 lines on 42 of the 45 pages -- the card could not see the closing line of nearly every front door it grades, and radiant-wishes-ending is a standing law of this tree.
think So neither existing rule is right, and the repair is a third: the register scan's marker-then-whitespace tests, plus a hold-out for a bold run closing on a colon with no terminal punctuation. A line ending in a full stop is a sentence whatever it opens with, so that clause carries its own discrimination.
think Measured the candidate in a mktemp pen against the real tree before touching a tracked file: 22 unchanged, 13 up, 10 down, mean +0.58, worst fall 5, best rise 8, no page crossing below B, and two rising above it that a blindness had held under.
obs The residue is named rather than swallowed. The hold-out reads a colon INSIDE the bold run, so the `**Standing witnesses** (twelve at tier lap): ...` form is still counted as prose -- 44 lines of 276, and the whole of amphora's 5-point fall. Telling a parenthetical from a sentence is a bigger question than this repair, so it is measured and left named.
obs Rewriting the control meant rewriting three legs whose whole premise was the fault. Leg 4b now asserts the repair and proves it bites from the failing side, restoring the elder pattern in a pen copy of the card and watching a four-sentence page collapse to one -- with a cmp check that the plant actually landed, which is %519's rule. Leg 4c's plant was repointed at header lines, since that is where the two rules now genuinely part. Leg 4d is new and proves both the radiant wish and the punctuation discrimination in both directions.
obs Against myself: the fifth link spelling fired again, on the lap after I named it. The elder card block copied onto a shelf inside construction/archive/ carries `](archive/...)`, written for the card's depth, and lands at archive/archive/. The QA card's own truth reading caught it at 80 before anything shipped. reds_fold.sh re-anchors links when it folds a REDS row; nothing does that for an ITINERARY account shelf, so it is a hand step every time, and it has now bitten twice in two laps.
